Cancel the actual courier booking on reversal, fix APC tracking link (v0.142)

Three asks from Dan's follow-up after v0.141:

1. "Cancel & Return to Stock" and "Reverse to Despatch" now attempt to void
   the actual courier shipment, not just BNS's own record of it. APC's own
   integration guide documents a CancelOrder endpoint (PUT Orders/{waybill}
   with Status=CANCELLED) that works right up until the point APC
   manifests the order - after that it's billed and can't be cancelled via
   their API, matching what Dan described ("especially [APC] charge for
   anything that's been manifested"). ApcShippingService.cancelOrder() adds
   this call, and OrderReversalService attempts it best-effort right before
   clearing apcWaybill/apcOrderNumber in both reversal methods - it never
   blocks the stock reversal itself, since that's the actual point of the
   operation. A failed attempt (overwhelmingly likely: already manifested)
   is surfaced to the frontend as a non-blocking warning so staff know to
   check APC's own portal if it matters.

   DPD has no equivalent - checked thoroughly this time by browsing the
   entire DPD docs portal (Shipping, Collections, Sender Actions, Receiver
   Actions, Pickup, Returns), not just the Shipping section as before.
   There is no shipment-level cancel/void endpoint anywhere in DPD's API;
   the only "cancel" is Cancel Collection, which only cancels a requested
   driver-attended pickup job, not a shipment. This lines up with what Dan
   expected going in ("not as big of a deal for DPD as they only charge us
   for what they scan") - nothing changes for DPD orders.

   Both reversal controller endpoints now return an OrderReversalResult
   (the order plus an optional courierWarning) instead of a bare Order.

2. Looked into whether either courier's API supports generating/printing
   manifests, as a possible admin tool. Neither does - manifesting is an
   automatic process on both couriers' own side (APC's docs only ever
   mention it as a status the order reaches, never something triggerable;
   same conclusion from DPD's full docs portal). Not something to build.

3. APC's public tracking link ("Track →" on the order screen and Delivery
   History) was sending the short 7-digit consignment number as the `id`
   query parameter. Per a real working link Dan supplied, it actually needs
   the full 22-digit waybill, plus the postcode lowercased (spaces become
   a literal +). Fixed in utils/tracking.ts's apcTrackingUrl() and its two
   call sites, which were both slicing the full value down to 7 digits
   before passing it in.

